    "category": "Bank and lender failure early warning",
    "description": "A disclosure-based early warning system that reads public filings, funding structure, regulatory thresholds and market signals to identify banks and lenders drifting toward distress. Historical diagnostics publish misses plus explicit claim-eligibility flags.",
    "operating_entity": "ai.de, a Udyam registered sole proprietorship, Jaipur, India",
    "access_model": "Public research, historical diagnostics, API, hosted MCP and CLI are open. Paid named-list software watches public India Failure Radar names and served US FDIC-board names without a customer book. Europe remains named case files. Fixed-scope proof pilots remain available for private-book validation.",
